  "body": "Re this example:\r\n\r\n> &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=​\"alexsalmond\\.jpeg\" alt=​\"\"&gt; Ahead of today's referendum,\r\n> the First Minister of Scotland, Alex Salmond, wrote an open letter to all\r\n> registered voters\\. In it, he admitted that all countries make mistakes\\.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n\r\nFrom https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/images.html#ancillary-images\r\n\r\nI'm unaware of the source of this example text and I couldn't find any evidence of the named politician writing this particular message.\r\n\r\nCould I please suggest that the example is changed to something more neutral? Additionally, I'm unsure of the wisdom of using a living person in examples.",
